import VOA.Modules.ZhuVermaAnArchUniversal

/-!
# `realizesIrr` from generation-from-bottom — the injective boss of Zhu Thm 5.3.4

`Modules.ZhuVermaAnArchUniversal` reduced the injective half of Zhu Theorem 5.3.4 — the Zhu
bijection `Φ(𝒱) ↔ Irr A(𝒱)` — to the bundled universal-property data `LUUniversalData W`, whose two
`Prop`-valued fields are

  `isoInvariant : ∀ U₁ U₂, U₁ ≅ U₂ → L(U₁) ≅ L(U₂)`   (functoriality of `L(·)` on bottoms)
  `realizesIrr  : ∀ P, P.IsIrreducibleLW → L(P.toAMod) ≅ P` (generation-from-bottom)

with `K = U ↦ L(U) = M(U)/J` the Dong–Jiang/Frenkel–Zhu generalized-Verma irreducible quotient
(`LUFamily.K`). This file is the **injective boss**: it proves the second clause `realizesIrr` from
the genuine *universal property of `M(U)`* (Frobenius reciprocity / generation-from-bottom),
reducing it to a single precise crux and wiring it into `LUUniversalData`.

## The strategy — the universal property / first isomorphism theorem

Fix an irreducible lowest-weight `P`. The universal property of the induced module `M(P.toAMod)`
says: the identity-on-the-bottom map `P.toAMod = P_h → P_h` lifts uniquely to a `𝒱`-module map

  `q : M(P.toAMod) → P`

(Frobenius reciprocity). Because `P` is **generated by its bottom** (lowest-weight + irreducible),
`q` is **surjective**; and its kernel `ker q` is a proper graded submodule of `M(P.toAMod)` meeting
the bottom trivially, hence is exactly the maximal `J = (ludata P.toAMod).J` (irreducibility of `P`
forces it to be maximal). Then the first isomorphism theorem gives, *unconditionally*,

  `L(P.toAMod) = M(P.toAMod)/J = M(P.toAMod)/ker q ≅ P`,

an isomorphism of `𝒱`-modules — exactly `LWModule.Iso (K P.toAMod) P`.

## What is built (axiom-clean)

The genuine deep content — the *existence* of the lifting `q`, its surjectivity, and the
identification `ker q = J` — is the Dong–Jiang/Frenkel–Zhu universal property. We carry **exactly**
that, and only that, as the hypothesis structure `RealizesIrrData F P` (a `𝒱`-intertwining ℂ-linear
map `q`, surjective, with `ker q = (F.ludata P.toAMod).J.carrier`), with no `sorry` and no axiom.
From it everything is **unconditional**:

* **`RealizesIrrData.iso`** — the `𝒱`-module isomorphism `L(P.toAMod) ≅ P` built by the first
  isomorphism theorem (`LinearMap.quotKerEquivOfSurjective`), with the mode-intertwining
  transported through the quotient action `quotient_act_mk`. This is `realizesIrr` for a single `P`,
  *proved* from the lifting data, not assumed.
* **`RealizesIrrData.lwIso`** — the same packaged as `LWModule.Iso W (F.K P.toAMod) P`.
* **`realizesIrr_of_realizesIrrFamily`** — the headline: from a per-`P` family of
  `RealizesIrrData`, the full `realizesIrr` clause of `LUUniversalData` holds.
* **`LUUniversalData.of_genFromBottom`** — assemble `LUUniversalData` from the `L(U)` family, the
  `isoInvariant` clause, and the `realizesIrr` lifting family — reducing the injective boss to its
  single genuine crux.
* **`zhuBijection_of_genFromBottom`** — the main Zhu bijection, resting on the lifting
  family (generation-from-bottom) as its sole injective-half input.

## The exact remaining crux

Everything above is unconditional given `RealizesIrrFamily F`. The single residual is, for each
irreducible `P`, the existence of the surjective bottom-identity lifting
`q : M(P.toAMod) → P` with `ker q = J` — the universal property / generation-from-bottom of
`M(U)`. It is carried as a `Prop`-valued / data hypothesis (the Frobenius reciprocity content of
DJ Prop 3.4–3.5 and Li §2), **never** an axiom; `#print axioms` on every proved theorem is
`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.

## References
Dong–Jiang, Math. Z. 259 (2008) (`math/0601626`), Prop 3.4–3.5, Thm 4.13; DLM3 §4;
H. Li hep-th/9406211 §2; Gannon §5.3.1–§5.3.2, Def. 5.3.1, Thm 5.3.4; Zhu [574]; Frenkel–Zhu.
-/

namespace VOA

open scoped BigOperators
open VertexOperatorAlgebra

universe u

variable {𝒱 : Type u} [AddCommGroup 𝒱] [Module ℂ 𝒱]

namespace InducedAssignment

variable {W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱}

/-! ## The lifting data — the universal property of `M(U)` for a single irreducible `P` -/

/-- **The generation-from-bottom lifting data for an irreducible `P`.**

This bundles the genuine Dong–Jiang/Frenkel–Zhu universal property of the induced module
`M(P.toAMod)` at the single irreducible lowest-weight module `P`:

* `q` — a ℂ-linear map `M(P.toAMod) → P` (the lift of the identity-on-the-bottom map, Frobenius
  reciprocity);
* `q_act` — `q` intertwines every mode (it is a `𝒱`-module homomorphism);
* `q_surjective` — `q` is surjective (`P` is generated by its bottom: lowest-weight + irreducible);
* `q_ker` — `ker q = J`, the maximal graded bottom-trivial submodule of `M(P.toAMod)` (forced by
  irreducibility of `P`).

This is *exactly* the content the universal property supplies; carried as a hypothesis structure,
with no `sorry` and **never** an axiom. The `𝒱`-iso `L(P.toAMod) ≅ P` is then unconditional. -/
structure RealizesIrrData (F : LUFamily W) (P : LWModule W) where
  /-- The lift `q : M(P.toAMod) → P` of the bottom-identity map (Frobenius reciprocity). -/
  q : MU W P.toAMod →ₗ[ℂ] P.carrier
  /-- `q` is a `𝒱`-module homomorphism: it intertwines every mode. -/
  q_act : ∀ (u : 𝒱) (n : ℤ) (x : MU W P.toAMod),
    q ((F.mudata P.toAMod).toOrdVModule.toWeakModule.act u n x)
      = P.isMod.toWeakModule.act u n (q x)
  /-- `q` is surjective (`P` is generated by its bottom). -/
  q_surjective : Function.Surjective q
  /-- `ker q = J`, the maximal bottom-trivial graded submodule. -/
  q_ker : LinearMap.ker q = (F.ludata P.toAMod).J.carrier

namespace RealizesIrrData

variable {F : LUFamily W} {P : LWModule W}

/-- The underlying linear equivalence `M(P.toAMod)/J ≅ P` from the first isomorphism theorem.

`q` is surjective, so `M(P.toAMod)/ker q ≅ P` (`LinearMap.quotKerEquivOfSurjective`). Since
`J = ker q` (`q_ker`), reindex the source `M(P.toAMod)/J = M(P.toAMod)/ker q`
(`Submodule.quotEquivOfEq`). The carrier of `F.K P.toAMod = L(P.toAMod) = M(P.toAMod)/J` is exactly
`MU W P.toAMod ⧸ (F.ludata P.toAMod).J.carrier`. -/
noncomputable def linEquiv (R : RealizesIrrData F P) :
    (MU W P.toAMod ⧸ (F.ludata P.toAMod).J.carrier) ≃ₗ[ℂ] P.carrier :=
  (Submodule.quotEquivOfEq _ _ R.q_ker.symm).trans (R.q.quotKerEquivOfSurjective R.q_surjective)

/-- On a representative coset `⟦x⟧`, the equivalence is `q x`. -/
@[simp] theorem linEquiv_mk (R : RealizesIrrData F P) (x : MU W P.toAMod) :
    R.linEquiv (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = R.q x := by
  unfold linEquiv
  rw [LinearEquiv.trans_apply, Submodule.quotEquivOfEq_mk,
    LinearMap.quotKerEquivOfSurjective_apply_mk]

/-- **The `𝒱`-module isomorphism `L(P.toAMod) ≅ P`.** The linear equivalence `linEquiv` intertwines
every mode: the action on `L(P.toAMod) = M(P.toAMod)/J` is `mkQ` of the `M(P.toAMod)`-action
(`quotient_act_mk`), and `q` intertwines that with the `P`-action (`q_act`). This is `realizesIrr`
for the single `P`, **proved** from the lifting data. -/
noncomputable def iso (R : RealizesIrrData F P) :
    ModuleEquiv W (F.K P.toAMod).isMod P.isMod where
  toLinearEquiv := R.linEquiv
  map_act u n x := by
    -- `x : MU ⧸ J`; reduce to a representative coset.
    refine Submodule.Quotient.induction_on _ x (fun z => ?_)
    -- The quotient action is `mkQ` of the `M(U)`-action (`quotient_act_mk`), then `linEquiv_mk`.
    -- `(F.K P.toAMod).isMod = (F.ludata P.toAMod).LU = OrdVModule.quotient … J J_graded`.
    change R.linEquiv ((F.K P.toAMod).isMod.toWeakModule.act u n (Submodule.Quotient.mk z))
      = P.isMod.toWeakModule.act u n (R.linEquiv (Submodule.Quotient.mk z))
    rw [show (F.K P.toAMod).isMod.toWeakModule.act u n (Submodule.Quotient.mk z)
          = Submodule.Quotient.mk
              ((F.mudata P.toAMod).toOrdVModule.toWeakModule.act u n z) from
        WeakModule.quotient_act_mk (F.mudata P.toAMod).toOrdVModule.toWeakModule
          (F.ludata P.toAMod).J u n z,
      R.linEquiv_mk, R.linEquiv_mk, R.q_act]

/-- **`L(P.toAMod) ≅ P` packaged as `LWModule.Iso`.** -/
theorem lwIso (R : RealizesIrrData F P) : LWModule.Iso W (F.K P.toAMod) P :=
  ⟨R.iso⟩

end RealizesIrrData

/-! ## The `realizesIrr` clause from the per-`P` lifting family -/

/-- **A per-irreducible-`P` family of generation-from-bottom lifting data.** For every irreducible
lowest-weight `P`, the universal-property lifting `RealizesIrrData F P`. This is the genuine deep
crux of the injective half of Theorem 5.3.4 (the universal property of `M(U)` / Frobenius
reciprocity for irreducibles); a hypothesis, **never** an axiom. -/
def RealizesIrrFamily (F : LUFamily W) : Type _ :=
  ∀ P : LWModule W, P.IsIrreducibleLW → RealizesIrrData F P

/-- **The `realizesIrr` clause from the lifting family.** Given the per-`P` lifting data
`RealizesIrrData F P` for every irreducible `P`, the second clause of `LUUniversalData` —
`∀ P, P.IsIrreducibleLW → L(P.toAMod) ≅ P` — holds, *unconditionally* (each iso is built by the
first isomorphism theorem from the lift). -/
theorem realizesIrr_of_realizesIrrFamily (F : LUFamily W) (R : RealizesIrrFamily F) :
    ∀ P : LWModule W, P.IsIrreducibleLW → LWModule.Iso W (F.K P.toAMod) P :=
  fun P hP => (R P hP).lwIso

/-! ## Assembling `LUUniversalData` and the Zhu bijection from generation-from-bottom -/

/-- **`LUUniversalData` from the `L(U)` family, the `isoInvariant` clause, and the lifting family.**

The injective boss reduced to its two genuine ingredients:

* `hiso` — functoriality of `L(·)` on bottoms (`isoInvariant`);
* `R` — the generation-from-bottom lifting family `RealizesIrrFamily F` (the universal property of
  `M(U)`), from which `realizesIrr` is *proved* via the first isomorphism theorem.

No `sorry`, no axiom. -/
noncomputable def LUUniversalData.of_genFromBottom (F : LUFamily W)
    (hiso : ∀ U₁ U₂ : AMod W, Nonempty (AModEquiv W U₁ U₂) → LWModule.Iso W (F.K U₁) (F.K U₂))
    (R : RealizesIrrFamily F) : LUUniversalData W where
  toLUFamily := F
  isoInvariant := hiso
  realizesIrr := realizesIrr_of_realizesIrrFamily F R

end InducedAssignment

/-- **The Zhu bijection `Φ(𝒱) ↔ Irr A(𝒱)` from generation-from-bottom.**

Packaging the end-to-end reduction with the injective half resting on the generation-from-bottom
lifting family: given the existence `InducedAssignment W` `A` producing irreducible realizations
(`hirr`), the ambient irreducibility scope (`hall`), the `L(U)` family `F`, the functoriality clause
`hiso`, and the lifting family `R : RealizesIrrFamily F` (the universal property of `M(U)`), the
forward map `forwardMap W` is a **bijection**. The injective half is located precisely in the
lifting family `R` — the genuine generation-from-bottom content of Zhu Theorem 5.3.4. -/
theorem zhuBijection_of_genFromBottom {W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱}
    (A : InducedAssignment W) (hall : InducedAssignment.AllLWIrreducible W)
    (hirr : A.RealizeIrreducible) (F : InducedAssignment.LUFamily W)
    (hiso : ∀ U₁ U₂ : AMod W, Nonempty (AModEquiv W U₁ U₂) →
      LWModule.Iso W (F.K U₁) (F.K U₂))
    (R : InducedAssignment.RealizesIrrFamily F) :
    Function.Bijective (forwardMap W) :=
  zhuBijection_of_LUUniversal A hall hirr
    (InducedAssignment.LUUniversalData.of_genFromBottom F hiso R)

end VOA

-- Axiom check (axiom-clean: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]).
